        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Kyiv</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 482 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">The date is debated: 482 CE is the traditional date, archaeological data indicates the 6th or 7th century, and some researchers date the founding as late as the late 9th century. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle">Primary Chronicle</a> the brothers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyi-shchek-and-khoryv">Kyi, Shchek and Khoryv</a> and their sister Lybid founded it.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">On both banks of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a> River in north-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, on the hills of the western bank, close to the mouth of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/desna-river">Desna</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">Capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus'</a>; the baptism of 988; St Sophia Cathedral and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv-pechersk-lavra">Monastery of the Caves</a>; the Mongol destruction of 1240; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv-mohyla-academy">Kyiv-Mohyla Academy</a>; capital of Soviet and then independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>; Babi Yar</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Kyiv is the capital and most populous city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>, a city with the legal status of a region.</span></div>
